\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of LaGarNet. \textcolor {revblue}{(a) Initial and goal states of simulated \text  {Cloth3D} garments \cite  {bertiche2020cloth3d} in our benchmark. (b) Real garments used for physical evaluation, \textcolor {irevgreen}{where the shape and material of the cream longsleeved dress (marked \emph  {Out of Distribution}) are unseen during training}. (c) The UR5e real-world setup with an OnRobot RG2 gripper; input images are taken by a top-down RealSense camera. (d) LaGarNet flattening a real dress: bright blue arrows are the mean of the action Gaussian in the early Model Predictive Control iterations and purple arrows the resulting final ones (top); the bottom row reports normalised coverage (NC), normalised improvement (NI), maximum IoU, the ground-truth reward and the prior reward predicted at the last planning step (all values multiplied by 100). Trained in simulation, our single-policy LaGarNet transfers zero-shot to the real world for flattening 4 different types of garments.}}}{1}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:LaGarNet}{{1}{1}{Overview of LaGarNet. \rev {(a) Initial and goal states of simulated \text {Cloth3D} garments \cite {bertiche2020cloth3d} in our benchmark. (b) Real garments used for physical evaluation, \irev {where the shape and material of the cream longsleeved dress (marked \emph {Out of Distribution}) are unseen during training}. (c) The UR5e real-world setup with an OnRobot RG2 gripper; input images are taken by a top-down RealSense camera. (d) LaGarNet flattening a real dress: bright blue arrows are the mean of the action Gaussian in the early Model Predictive Control iterations and purple arrows the resulting final ones (top); the bottom row reports normalised coverage (NC), normalised improvement (NI), maximum IoU, the ground-truth reward and the prior reward predicted at the last planning step (all values multiplied by 100). Trained in simulation, our single-policy LaGarNet transfers zero-shot to the real world for flattening 4 different types of garments.}}{figure.caption.1}{}}
